  "name": "Microfilaria Test QBC",
  "code": "MF",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ol><li><p>Positive: If microfilariae are detected in the blood sample, it indicates an active infection with filarial parasites. The specific species of microfilariae detected can help identify the type of filarial infection, such as Wuchereria bancrofti, Brugia malayi, or Onchocerca volvulus.</p></li><li><p>Negative: If no microfilariae are seen in the blood sample, it suggests the absence of active microfilarial infection at the time of testing. However, it's important to note that a negative result does not completely rule out the presence of filarial infection, as microfilariae may be intermittently present in the bloodstream.</p></li></ol>",
